This looks like August 2019. The 10-year yield is 1.50%, the fed funds rate is 2.12% after the July cut, and the 2s10s spread is about -0.03. Long Treasuries returned +8.9% in the month, gold is up 5.4%, and unemployment is 3.7%. Core CPI at 2.21% and headline at 1.81% also fit 2019.

The equity returns fit August as well: large caps were down 0.8% in the month, and emerging markets were down 1.9%.

